  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1948\n£10.00\n\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1948 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Brigadier-General C. G. Higgins, C.M.G., D.S.O. Volume L January to December 1948.\n\nPublished 1949 - Slatter & Rose Oxford. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nRecords of the First Battalion\n\nSummary of the First Battalion Diary\n\nFirst Battalion Letter\n\nIncident on Border of Anglo-Soviet Zones, First Battalion\n\nSignalling, First Battalion\n\nAthletics, First Battalion\n\nBoxing, First Battalion\n\nCricket, First Battalion\n\nHockey, First Battalion\n\nFootball, First Battalion\n\nWeapon Training, First Battalion\n\nShooting, First Battalion\n\nRacing and Horse Shows, First Battalion\n\nRecords of Regimental Headquarters\n\nHeadquarters Letter\n\nRecords of the Fourth Battalion\n\nFourth Battalion Letter\n\nExtracts from the London Gazette\n\nThe Land of the Rising Sun\n\nThe Freedom Ceremonies\n\nThe Freedom of Aylesbury\n\nThe War Rocket\n\nAgricultural Shows\n\nSouthern Africa Revisited\n\nPostman's Progress\n\nKenya Coast\n\nThe Flintlock Musket in Wet Weather\n\nThose Were The Days\n\nThe Regimental Dinner\n\nThe Regimental Luncheon\n\nThe 43rd (Mesopotamia Dinner)\n\nThe 52nd Luncheon\n\n2nd Bucks Battalion Dinner\n\nRegimental Cricket Week\n\nOld Comrades Association\n\nObituary\n\nIndex\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nThe Skipper’s War: Dragon School, Oxford & The Great War\n£20.00 Add to cart\nMister Brownrigg’s Boys: Magdalen College School and the Great War\n£15.00 Add to cart\nThe Story of the Oxfordshire Yeomanry – Queen’s Own Oxfordshire Hussars 1798-1998\n£7.95 Read more\nChildren and War – A Bugle & Sabre Special\n£2.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
